                <head>No. 571.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville
                            West to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-04-17"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 17,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>With reference to the supplementary convention concluded at Washington on the 6th
                    of December, 1884, between the Governments of the United States and Hawaii, Her
                    Majesty’s Government call attention to the treaty of 10th of July, 1851, between
                    Great Britain and Hawaii, which provides for access of British ships of war to
                    all harbors, rivers, and places within the territories of Hawaii, and to anchor
                    there and relit.</p>
                <p>Her Majesty’s Government have never sought any exclusive advantages under this
                    treaty, but in view of the provisions of the above-mentioned convention
                    respecting Pearl River Harbor, they have reminded the Hawaiian Government of
                    this treaty, and inform the United States Government that they have done so.</p>
            </div>
